    {
      "occurrenceId": "36f2ff55db7cdcc74f1d1de685efc7b6a898b8dafa212f349284220746c19673",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/0"
      },
      "text": "Allocation-level footprint invariance (independent, hybrid) does NOT confer learning-level footprint invariance. At resolving quantization no law has a footprint-invariant focal edge.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "4c2950e114aededc8ef413df17d75b109f38e442a3933e71b2db61f66bbe8dbf",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/1"
      },
      "text": "The ~1/n per-edge dependence is common to all four laws and is therefore not the RET-001 defect. For the three derived laws it follows from a conserved attentional resource divided among n partners, which is the intended behaviour.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "d7d3147cbec12d1870c4b05cd240e94c2d9ce9cc844db89419028aea552c5df6",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/2"
      },
      "text": "The RET-001 defect is budget saturation: flat tagging consumes 100% of the associative row budget at every footprint and overflows from n=2, so total learned mass carries no information about the focal evidence. The three derived laws hold total mass essentially constant and evidence-proportional.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "7aa6dce7673c6dd68d7eb3a5783948318e8e473041ef67373e09641014d3d784",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/3"
      },
      "text": "MEC-005 residual-pool conservation is load-bearing for MEC-007 shared allocation: shared z_focal degrades monotonically with footprint only in the unconserved regime.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "3cd9488fb6ab9283d8651e70b6ba3422d142b68a9ba1b35f3a44632cad7bfe26",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/4"
      },
      "text": "A quantization-floor artifact is visible and is reported rather than suppressed: at D=100 the independent focal edge is zero at every footprint, which reads as invariance and is not.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "b5d6bc0eb2903474a6c7d136f1280c7e92f429c3af528750528dc48f33211a33",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/0"
      },
      "text": "Pure arithmetic. No identity, canonical record, allocation, record type, public ingress, state writer, source admission or corpus promotion.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "3d8dbeead3b7e4d784f6ba5c2f90fa0c19b5d0338deedf9c422f0fb89964bbc5",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/1"
      },
      "text": "Establishes which laws are behaviourally distinguishable, and isolates the retired control. Does NOT establish which of the three derived laws is psychologically correct — that needs the encoding -> later-retrieval probe, BLOCKED on its own seam.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "89f53ae4425b576df925725cb8bc48657daa6711b69d9ce30ea9b6316ba17930",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/2"
      },
      "text": "MEC-005 stays CONTROL+CONTRACT; MEC-007/CTL-004 stay CONTROL; MEC-008 stays CONTROL with its sole-writer and largest-remainder invariants; RET-001 stays retired, executable only as this named negative comparison.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "71445d328033a96328d1bd432940c49469ca6d4ff505dd7d309f9f167481999f",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/3"
      },
      "text": "One focal evidence vector, one incidental profile, one prior graph (empty), eta=1, no decay. Richer priors, several focal units and nonzero decay are untested.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "452c2fbdd83457d6ae95e39d69ff2c2956d7cf9a090f4593612aff41dfee02d5",
      "source": "docs/planning/SALIENCE_LAW_COMPARISON_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "bbe58ca1dd43f114c3af4f705df9df8630b686af25a50df6f3d2dc52f4ff0a37",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/4"
      },
      "text": "A hard top-K selector still does not establish a continuous salience law; the bounded public ATTN profile is unchanged.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    }
  ],
